## llvm-cil-dump on malformed images (plan 5.7.8, 5.7.10, 5.7.12): every
## damage is an error with its prefix ('invalid CLI image: ' from the PE
## reader, 'invalid CLI metadata: ' from the metadata reader), reported as
## 'llvm-cil-dump: error: '<file>': <message>' with exit status 1, never a
## crash or an assertion (section 2: the guards against 'LLVM ERROR' and
## 'PLEASE submit' catch an abort(), which plain 'not' accepts on Windows).
## mkbad.py derives the variants from a yaml2obj copy of the ilasm (.NET
## Framework 4.8, -dll -pe64 -x64) image of exit42.il.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# RUN: yaml2obj %t/exit42.yaml -o %t/exit42.dll
# RUN: %python %t/mkbad.py %t/exit42.dll %t

## The unmodified image is fine.
